{"name":"Hot Pink","hex":"#ff028d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hot pink","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bright vibrant pink colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a bright vibrant pink colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hot_pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hot Pink (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Hot Pink is the second studio album by American rapper and singer Doja Cat. It was released on November 7, 2019, by Kemosabe Records and RCA Records. A departure from the sound of her debut album Amala (2018), Hot Pink is a pop, hip-hop, and R&B record containing elements of funk and soul. The album features production from Doja herself, Yeti Beats, Tyson Trax, and others, with guest appearances from Smino, Gucci Mane, and Tyga."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/87/Doja_Cat_-_Hot_Pink.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_Pink_(album)","wikidata":"Q75107008"},{"title":"Hot Pink (The Pink Spiders album)","blocks":[{"text":"Hot Pink is the debut studio album by American band the Pink Spiders, released in 2005."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/63/Hot_Pink_Spiders.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_Pink_(The_Pink_Spiders_album)","wikidata":"Q5910217"},{"title":"Shades of pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink colors are usually light or desaturated shades of reds, roses, and magentas which are created on computer and television screens using the RGB color model and in printing with the CMYK color model. As such, it is an arbitrary classification of color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Color_icon_pink_v2.svg/330px-Color_icon_pink_v2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_pink","wikidata":"Q19847189"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Miriam_Makeba_%281969%29.jpg/500px-Miriam_Makeba_%281969%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Miriam_Makeba_%281969%29.jpg/1280px-Miriam_Makeba_%281969%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Miriam_Makeba_%281969%29.jpg/500px-Miriam_Makeba_%281969%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMiriam_Makeba_(1969).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Blink-182_at_the_Showcase_Theater_in_Corona_July_18%2C1995.jpg/500px-Blink-182_at_the_Showcase_Theater_in_Corona_July_18%2C1995.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Blink-182_at_the_Showcase_Theater_in_Corona_July_18%2C1995.jpg/1280px-Blink-182_at_the_Showcase_Theater_in_Corona_July_18%2C1995.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Blink-182_at_the_Showcase_Theater_in_Corona_July_18%2C1995.jpg/500px-Blink-182_at_the_Showcase_Theater_in_Corona_July_18%2C1995.jpg?u